title the guards our own rules demand -- five rule-named guards join the roster, and the report card learns to print its own scale
prompt The HUSH seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5 advancing by hand past a repeat, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves, claim-as-override when my lane's queue is empty. My own last recommend named the door: the 41 silent choirs of %360.
think LISTAGENTS FIRST, and it answered none reachable. No peer named, no file of anyone else's touched; the commit stays path-limited and the amend stands behind the empty-index check.
think REDS FIRST. One row reads OPEN on the living pin and it is %360, mine from last lap. Nothing else was agent-closable, so the standfast and the constructive door were the same door.
think ROTA. N=3826 by git rev-list --count HEAD gives row 1, AIR -- law and boundary, whose sense is touch. Last lap read row 2, so no repeat and I took the arithmetic row. The threshold page says a claim of a boundary is tested by pressing on it, and where the hand passes through, the boundary was a wish. That is %360 in one sentence: the roster is a claim about coverage, %360 pressed on it, and the hand went through 1,153 times.
think THE DOOR THE CARD NAMED, AND WHAT MEASURING IT CHANGED. The card said the 41 silent choirs, so I measured what each would actually buy -- the marginal hearing gain of adding that choir alone to the roster, closed to fixpoint. The top of that list is cion_module_labeling at 21, then equinox_e110 at 20, drey at 17. Then I read who owns them, and the answer redirected the lap: %360 already measured a 46% red rate across this population, and its own log records that the 21 reds live in Glow, STOA, SUNN and the equinox family -- lanes this seat does not hold. Rostering another lane's red guard reds every body's cold pass, which is the exact reason the roster's own auditor still waits at gate %7.
think SO THE SUBSET THAT IS MINE IS NOT THE BIGGEST ONE. Six of the 1,153 are guards a LIVING RULE in this tree instructs a lap to run: commit_message_guard (git-signing.md), mechanism_sentence (mechanism-sentence.md), sel4_userlevel_license (gratitude-licenses.md, which calls it "a standing check, not a one-time read"), waymark_derive and waymark_registry (waymark-ladders.md), and crypto_vendored_parity (docs/CRYPTO.md and the loop seed). A rule that names a check and a roster that never runs it are one sentence disagreeing with itself.
think THE COUNT IS NOT THE VALUE, and I want this written down because the card's phrasing invites the opposite. All six together buy 9 guards of hearing where one CION choir buys 21. What a rostered guard is worth is what breaks while it is silent, and these are the ones a rule already promised would not be silent.
think GREEN BEFORE ROSTERED, PROVEN RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Five ran GREEN on metal: waymark_derive 1s, commit_message_guard 2s, waymark_registry 3s, sel4_userlevel_license 0s, crypto_vendored_parity 12s. Eighteen seconds together against a cold pass of 2,425s, which is 0.7% and is why all five are tier lap rather than cadence. I had expected crypto_vendored_parity to be a cadence row and it is not -- it names crypto_suite only in comments and never runs it.
think HOLD STILL WHILE IT RUNS, AND THEN CHECK WHY. A cold pass was already in flight when I opened -- 19 minutes in, my own lock from last lap holding it -- so I read rather than wrote for the first half of the lap. Before running any candidate beside it I checked the one hazard that mattered: waymark_registry_verify.sh writes tools/.cache/waymark/corpus.txt, which is INSIDE the tree. It is gitignored at .gitignore:323 and tree_digest reads git rev-parse HEAD plus git status --porcelain, which excludes ignored files, so it cannot move the digest. I verified porcelain read 0 before and after every candidate run.
obs THE SIXTH IS REFUSED BY MEASUREMENT, NOT BY LANE, AND THE REASON IS ONE LAYER PAST WHAT %360 RECORDED. mechanism_sentence_witness reds on metal at line 57, WALL_EXEMPTS_SEED_ROOT. The row read this as "the breakage stood because the guard is unrostered." The sharper fact: the wall exempts the seed root at a subject spelled exactly crashed-meteor, and BOTH publish-seed.sh AND the wall's own fixture tools/fixtures/m/mechanism_wall_scan.sh write Grain OS -- initial public seed. Three sites agree and the wall alone moved on 20260828. So the fixture the witness trusts is refused by the wall it tests, the witness would have caught this the day it was rostered, and the spelling is custody gate %1.
obs MY OWN RED, CAUGHT BY READING THE TOOL RATHER THAN THE CARD. Grading the roster I passed --service 3, reading the card's "four questions" as a score out of four. The flag is on the same 0-100 scale as every other reading -- composite is (register + reach + truth + service + 2) / 4 -- so 3 meant 3/100 and the card read C+ 76, which under the standing block pushes a molt frame. Judged honestly the same file reads A+ 99. A grade that decides whether work happens must not be able to be mis-scaled in silence, and the usage line writes only [--service N].
obs A SECOND RED FOUND, PROVEN, AND DELIBERATELY NOT BOOKED THIS LAP. `tree_digest` in the roster runner is `git rev-parse HEAD` plus `git status --porcelain`, hashed. Porcelain prints a status letter and a path, never content -- so a content edit to a file ALREADY carrying `M` leaves the digest identical, and `tree_moved=no` is printed over a tree that did move. I did not reason this out; the instrument told me. I killed a hot pass, edited `construction/ITINERARY.md`, restarted, and both passes printed `tree_at_open=94b56275df59`. Then I proved it in a throwaway git repository rather than trusting the coincidence: a staged file rewritten twice gives one digest, while a NEW file moves it. So the guard catches a file appearing or changing status and misses the case it most exists for -- a hand editing a staged file during a forty-minute pass. It is not booked here because `construction/REDS.md` sits 57 bytes from its enforced bound, so the row wants a fold first, and because the repair changes the runner every body depends on and deserves its own control the way %359's lock got eleven behaviours. Naming it in one lap and fixing it in the next is the discipline; naming it nowhere would have been the red.
obs WHAT THAT FINDING COST ME, SAID PLAINLY. It cost two killed hot passes and roughly three minutes, because the honest move on finding the blind spot was to stop rather than to use it: my own session log was staged, and editing a staged file mid-pass is exactly the edit the digest cannot see. Shipping a tree the pass never measured, while knowing the guard is blind to it, would have made this log a false witness about itself.
obs NAMING A RETIRED COUNTER ON THE LIVING CARD IS USING IT, and I proved that the expensive way. The rebase surfaced `waymark_rung_drift` red from a bare `TUBE0` in `src/shape/README.md`, which arrived with upstream's `shape:` commits -- so I named it on the card as a sibling find, in Sound's lane, not touched. Sound then repaired the original while I was verifying, and the guard STILL read two past its ceiling: my own card note had written the token twice, and `construction/ITINERARY.md` is living prose the scan reads. Removing my two mentions took the reading from 17,245 to exactly 17,243 of 17,243. Session logs, counsel, waymarks, and bron-resins are excluded from that scan as testimony, which is why this line may spell the token and the card may not. The lesson is sharper than the fix: a guard over a retired FORM cannot be told about its own violations in the room it guards.
obs THREE REBASES, THREE RENUMBERS, AND THE LAW DID ALL THE WORK. Dream and Sound pushed thirteen commits across my lap. My row's number moved %361 -> %365 -> %370 because each time the anointed spine had spent mine, and each time the answer was mechanical: the stamp is the identity, a published number never moves, an unshared row derives above. I never had to decide anything -- I read `reds_spine_derive_scan.sh --next` after each fetch and the ledger headline republished with it. That is REDS %230/%252/%283 not happening, four times in one afternoon.
obs WHAT THIS DOES NOT REACH. Whether a rostered guard asserts anything worth asserting -- this lap moved five guards from unheard to heard and proved each green once, which is a different claim from proving each is a good guard. The other 1,144 stand where they stood. And the lane-safe choirs are measured but untaken: drey 17, acme_dx 11, operations_conformance 6, tensegral_arc_ii 5 -- named here so the measurement outlives the lap.
