file construction/standing-equipment.kyri five rule-named guards seated at tier lap, each GREEN on metal first; the unheard note accretes the re-measured reading beside the elder
file tools/fixtures/u/unheard_guard_scan.sh the ceiling falls 1153 to 1144 and the choir ceiling 41 to 40, by what the roster rows actually moved
file tools/u/unheard_guard_witness.rish the two literal ceiling asserts fall with the scan, in one commit, since they are the ratchet's teeth
file tools/fixtures/w/witness_reach_scan.sh unreached 1108 to 1093 and families 220 to 218, the fall recorded with its reason beside the elder falls
file tools/fixtures/q/qa_report_card.sh the judged reading prints service_scale on every run, in both branches, and the usage line names 0-100 (%361)
file tools/q/qa_report_card_witness.rish two runs of the real card assert the scale line, proven load-bearing by deleting it and watching the witness red by name
file construction/REDS.md %361 booked and closed on that witness; %360 accretes the five-row repair and stays OPEN; the headline republished 360 to 361
file construction/ITINERARY.md the Standing block restores "worth 25 each", the Now and live front carry the fallen ratchet, and the lane-safe choir gains are named so the measurement outlives the lap
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- FIVE GUARDS OUR OWN RULES ALREADY DEMANDED NOW RUN, FOR 18 SECONDS A LAP. `commit_message_guard`, `waymark_derive`, `waymark_registry`, `sel4_userlevel_license`, and `crypto_vendored_parity` stand on the roster at `tier lap`, each proven GREEN on metal BEFORE its row was written, because rostering a red guard reds every body's cold pass. `unheard` falls 1,153 -> 1,144, choirs 41 -> 40, `witness_reach` unreached 1,103 -> 1,093 and families 220 -> 218, every ceiling falling with the reading in the same commit. THE COUNT WAS NOT THE VALUE, and that is why the lap took this five rather than the biggest choir: all five together buy 9 guards of hearing where one CION choir buys 21, yet what a rostered guard is worth is what breaks while it is silent, and these are the ones a rule already promised would not be silent. The cheapest was the most overdue -- `gratitude-licenses.md` calls the seL4 sweep a standing check, and no standing pass had ever run it. YOUR GATE IS NOW ONE WORD, AND SHARPER THAN %360 RECORDED IT. `mechanism_sentence_witness` reds on metal at `WALL_EXEMPTS_SEED_ROOT`. The wall exempts the seed root at a subject spelled exactly `crashed-meteor`; `publish-seed.sh` AND the wall's own fixture `tools/fixtures/m/mechanism_wall_scan.sh` BOTH write `Grain OS -- initial public seed`. Three sites agree and the wall alone moved on `20260828`, so the fixture the witness trusts is refused by the wall it tests -- meaning that guard would have caught this the day it was rostered, and it cannot join the roster until you say the spelling. Custody gate %1, surfaced rather than chosen. I ALSO BOOKED AND CLOSED ONE OF MY OWN (%361). Grading the roster I handed in `--service 3`, reading the card's own "four questions" as a score out of four; the flag is 0-100, so the tool read 3 of 100 and returned C+ 76 on a file that reads A+ 99 -- and a below-B reading pushes a molt frame, so the instrument the fleet grades itself with could turn an honest judgment into invented work. The scale lived in exactly one place, the loop's seat prompt ("worth 25 each"), and this card, two rules, and the usage line all dropped it. The card now prints `service_scale` beside `service` in both branches, the rostered witness asserts it, and I proved that assert load-bearing by deleting the line and watching the witness red by name. YOUR OTHER GATES ARE UNCHANGED: `rule_twin` still reds at %7, which still keeps the roster's own auditor off the roster; Pond `entry` is still the switchover at %5. MINE NEXT, and it is a red before it is a lap: `tree_digest` cannot see a content edit to an already-modified file, so `tree_moved=no` promises less than it reads -- proven in a pen this lap, unbooked because REDS sits 57 bytes from its bound and the repair touches the runner every body shares, so it wants a fold and its own control. Then the lane-safe choirs, gains already measured -- `drey` 17, `acme_dx` 11, `operations_conformance` 6 -- run on metal first, rostered only where green.
